*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- numbering clean-up
* RMVUNUSED deletes the 72 separate nodes no element uses (interior positions of z = -6 and -2 off
* the two interior walls); NCOM then closes the gaps (CHECK warns about every missing number).
* Nodes 1-648 keep their numbers; the separate nodes become 649-772:
*     z = -6: 649-661 and z = -2: 711-723 (interior-wall nodes)
*     z = -4: node = 654 + 7 j + i   and   z = 0: node = 716 + 7 j + i      (i, j = 1..7)
RMVUNUSED
NCOM
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- drilling rotations
* A flat shell has no stiffness about its normal.  FIXROT fixes that rotation at the nodes connected
* to shells alone (the superstructure and the separate basement nodes) and the rotations of the
* nodes connected to solids alone.  It does not act on nodes shared by shells and excavated solids:
* at the face-interior nodes of the basemat (normal Z) and of the outer basement walls at z = -6 and
* -2 (normal Y or X) the rotation about the normal is fixed with D, row by row (first and last
* node of each row); where a wall or a slab meets the face, its bending restrains that rotation.
FIXROT
VAR,BS,11,15,20,24,29,33,47,51,56,60,65,69
VAR,BE,13,17,22,26,31,35,49,53,58,62,67,71
FOREACH,BS,D,@BS[#],@BE[#],1,1,ROTZ
VAR,YS,83,87,245,249,155,159,317,321
VAR,YE,85,89,247,251,157,161,319,323
FOREACH,YS,D,@YS[#],@YE[#],1,1,ROTY
VAR,XS,91,127,253,289,99,135,261,297
VAR,XE,109,145,271,307,117,153,279,315
FOREACH,XS,D,@XS[#],@XE[#],9,1,ROTX
